---
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';
import KnowledgeField from '../components/KnowledgeField.astro';
import graph from '../../public/graphs/working/tensor.core.graph.json';
import catalog from '../../public/graphs/working/event-profiles/catalog.json';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../data/seo';

const meta = seo.home;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebSite',
  name: 'TENSOR',
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, '/'),
  description: meta.description,
};
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} hidePageTitle={true} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="section-hero">
    <div class="hero-content container">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <p class="hero-kicker">Cyber investigation / Public standard initiative</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title">A common language for <span>investigation.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-definition"><strong>Shared questions, evidence, and decisions.</strong><br />TENSOR connects investigation questions, evidence, and decisions in a shared record for humans and agents. Vendors and companies add their own graphs above the public foundation.</p>
        <div class="cta-group">
          <Button variant="primary" href="/start/" data-telemetry-event="cta-open-start" data-telemetry-location="home-hero">Start here · TENSOR in five minutes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></Button>
          <Button variant="secondary" href="/graphs/?renderer=3d" data-telemetry-event="cta-open-graph" data-telemetry-location="home-hero">Graph atlas <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></Button>
        </div>
        <p class="candidate-status">IMPLEMENTATION CANDIDATE<br /><a href="/review/">Core 0.1.0-draft.1 · Current public dataset</a></p>
      </div>
      <KnowledgeField />
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="home-register container" aria-label="Working investigation knowledge">
    <p class="register-label">Public investigation<br />knowledge</p>
    <a href="/graphs/"><strong>{graph.nodes.length}</strong><span>Working questions</span></a>
    <a href="/graphs/"><strong>{String(new Set(graph.nodes.map(node => node.category)).size).padStart(2, '0')}</strong><span>Investigation domains</span></a>
    <a href="/graphs/profiles/"><strong>{Object.keys(catalog.profiles).length}</strong><span>Event profiles</span></a>
  </div>

  <section class="home-section home-architecture" aria-labelledby="layers-title">
    <div class="container architecture-grid">
      <div class="architecture-copy">
        <p class="section-kicker">01 / Vendor and organization graphs</p>
        <h2 id="layers-title">Public knowledge.<br />Specialized graphs.</h2>
        <p>The public graph supplies technical questions and evidence criteria. Vendor graphs add product knowledge, data-source mappings, and collection checks. Organization graphs add policy, ownership, escalation, and workflow.</p>
        <p>Each layer has an owner, version, and declared dependencies. Technical findings remain distinguishable from product procedures and business decisions.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/extensions/">Vendor and organization layering guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="layer-stack" role="img" aria-label="Human and agent investigators use vendor and organization graphs above the public investigation graph and TENSOR Core. Core connects pinned definitions with portable records.">
        <div class="layer-actors"><span>Human investigators</span><b>+</b><span>Agent investigators</span></div>
        <div class="layer-pair"><div><strong>Vendor graph</strong><small>Product questions,<br />evidence mappings, integrations</small></div><div><strong>Organization graph</strong><small>Policy, ownership,<br />escalation, workflow</small></div></div>
        <div class="layer-public"><strong>Public investigation graph</strong><small>Technical questions, evidence criteria, event profiles</small></div>
        <div class="layer-core"><strong>TENSOR Core</strong><small>Shared investigative meaning<br />Pinned definitions + portable records</small></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section container" aria-labelledby="example-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="section-kicker">02 / Investigation records</p>
      <div><h2 id="example-title">Questions, evidence, and a retained history.</h2><p>An investigation record connects each assessment to its question, evidence, context, and author. Revisions preserve the earlier record.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="investigation-example">
      <div class="example-intro">
        <span class="case-number">INVESTIGATION / AGENT ACTION</span>
        <h3>Did the agent send restricted information?</h3>
        <p>This reference case records an outbound tool call, an initially unknown content assessment, new evidence, and a revised finding.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/investigation-lab/">Open the reference case <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <ol class="example-trace">
        <li><span class="trace-type">Question context</span><p>A specific agent, outbound call, time window, and policy context.</p></li>
        <li><span class="trace-type">Initial assessment</span><p>The call is visible; the transmitted content is not yet established.</p></li>
        <li><span class="trace-type">Revised assessment</span><p>A receipt changes the assessment. The earlier entry and its inputs remain.</p></li>
        <li><span class="trace-type">Decision record</span><p>The selected assessment, rationale, policy reference, and claimed authority are recorded separately from any execution.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="section-features" aria-label="What Core preserves">
      <article class="feature-card"><span>01</span><h3>Questions with context</h3><p>A versioned definition describes the question. Each instance binds it to particular subjects, parameters, and time.</p></article>
      <article class="feature-card"><span>02</span><h3>Unknowns and disagreement</h3><p>Missing evidence, bounded negative findings, and competing assessments have distinct representations.</p></article>
      <article class="feature-card"><span>03</span><h3>Portable investigation history</h3><p>Evidence references, attribution, original inputs, and revisions travel with the record. Exchange reports identify omissions and unsupported meaning.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>



  <section class="home-section container" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="section-kicker">03 / Tools and implementation</p><div><h2 id="start-title">Implementation resources.</h2><p>Reference tools cover question exploration, record exchange, and graph layering. The Core applies across cyber investigation domains.</p></div></div>
    <div class="home-entry-list">
      <a class="home-entry" href="/start/"><span>00</span><h3>TENSOR in five minutes</h3><p>A suspicious sign-in investigation, from the first alert to a handoff, with human, agent, vendor, and company roles.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="home-entry" href="/investigation-lab/"><span>01</span><h3>Investigation Lab</h3><p>Example cases, local bundle validation, recorded-path replay, and import/export.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="home-entry" href="/implement/"><span>02</span><h3>Implementation guide</h3><p>A browser workflow, pinned command-line baseline, integration roles, and versioned artifacts.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="home-entry" href="/graphs/"><span>03</span><h3>Graph atlas</h3><p>All 609 current questions, evidence criteria, guided paths, and 3D exploration from the shared public dataset.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="home-entry" href="/extensions/"><span>04</span><h3>Vendor and organization graphs</h3><p>Layer responsibilities, downloadable examples, and a working cloud-layer preview.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-review">
    <div class="container">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">04 / Specification and review</p><h2>An open specification.<br />A reproducible baseline.</h2></div>
      <div><p>The specification includes 38 proposed Core requirements, a JSON binding, schemas, reference cases, and a pinned technical review package. Standards relationships cover ATT&amp;CK, D3FEND, ATLAS, CASE/UCO, STIX, Attack Flow, CACAO, and OCSF.</p><div class="cta-group"><Button variant="primary" href="/review/">Technical review package <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></Button><a class="text-link" href="/standards/">Standards relationships <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="review-status">Core 0.1.0-draft.1 · Unratified candidate<br />Independent review and exchange remain open.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
